OL,3,GNEWSASouthport families 'blown away' by
OL,4,Asupport for memorial garden
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe families of the three girls killed
OL,7,Fin the Southport attack said they have
OL,8,Fbeen "blown away" by support for plans
OL,9,Fto create a memorial in Southport's
OL,10,Ftown hall gardens.
OL,12,FRelatives of Alice Aguiar, Bebe King
OL,13,Fand Elsie Stancombe welcomed feedback
OL,14,Fon proposals to regenerate the area in
OL,15,Ffront of the town hall and Atkinson art
OL,16,Fgallery.
OL,18,FAbout 300 people took part in Sefton
OL,19,FCouncil's consultation on the scheme,
OL,20,Fwhich would include a landscaped
OL,21,Fperformance space in tribute to the
OL,22,Fgirls.
OL,23,APub: 23-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB NW Eng NewsC Reg TVF Weather
FL,406,400,260,160,0,100
